    kind: work_item  # 1937
    title: "python: route the tracked receiver type into the module slot so #231's edges can reach callees_at (INV-linub instance)"  # 1937
    status: todo_hard  # 1937
    priority: 2  # 1937
    parent:  # 1937
    tags:  # 1937
    - taint  # 1937
    - adr_0017  # 1937
    - analysis_quality  # 1937
    - io_boundary  # 1937
    isbefore: []  # 1937
    duplicate_of: []  # 1937
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 1937
    pr_ref:  # 1937
    description: "INSTANCE OF THE INV-linub CLASS, for python, on the SECOND consumer of L3\n(receiver evidence) that the class statement does not name.\n\nWHAT IS WRONG. PR #231 taught py.py to emit a call edge for an attribute chain\nrooted at a local -- voucher_list.append(x), p.save(...), payment.confirm().\nIt hardcodes the dst as python:external:0-0:NAME:unresolved, and its own\ncomment explains why: \"the receiver's type is genuinely unknown here\", and\ninventing a module would assert something false. Correct at that branch.\n\nBut the \"external\" placeholder in the module slot makes the edge USELESS\ndownstream. _module_from_symbol_path returns \"\" for the placeholder BY\nDOCUMENTED DESIGN, so _qualified_callee yields no key, so\n_catalogue_key_for_edge yields None, so the (function, line) never enters\ncallees_at, so _use_site_terminates cannot decide, so the section 3a walk\nrecords an ESCAPE. The edge is emitted and then discarded.\n\nMEASURED (2026-08-06, scripts/measure-call-escape-cause.py, positive control\npassed -- pretix: 443,296 edges offered, 191,264 accepted, 69 summary entries,\n31,913 callees_at entries): on pretix, 13 of 17 call-node escape sites (76.5%)\nare exactly this, and ZERO lack an edge. save, confirm, delete, get,\nrefresh_from_db, create_external_refund, log_action, append, create.\n\nWHY THIS IS THE JAVA SHAPE. PR #227 fixed the identical defect for java: the\ninferred receiver type \"was already in var_types, routed only to meta\", and the\nfix routed it into the module slot instead. py.py carries var_types AND\nexternal_var_types. The question this item must answer FIRST is whether either\nis reachable at the #231 emit site for the chain root -- if it is not, this is a\nlarger change than #227 was and should be re-scoped before being attempted.\n\n*** DIRECTION, AND IT IS THE DANGEROUS ONE. *** Giving these calls a qualified\nkey lets _use_site_terminates return True more often, which produces MORE False\nverdicts, and since PR #214 a False earns sanitized and DROPS the flow from the\nviolation set. This is a SUPPRESSIVE change. Two measured counterweights, both\nof which must be re-checked before landing rather than taken from this note:\n  1. Of the three pretix sites that DID get a key, two hit \"no summary\" and one\n     hit \"propagates\". None closed. So the empirical suppression on this corpus\n     is small.\n  2. There are ZERO barrier-arm walks on all four repos that produce walks\n     (hypergumbo 36, pretix 35, prometheus 7, alertmanager 3 -- every\n     invocation on the 3a arm, where False and None collapse). So today this\n     change cannot move a finding in EITHER direction.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR PRIORITY: this is a capability fix with a measured-zero blast\nradius, which makes it cheap and safe NOW and dangerous LATER -- the hazard\narms when a sanitizer catalogue exists. It is filed at P2 rather than P1\nbecause it moves no finding today; it is filed rather than skipped because the\nwindow in which it is safe closes.\n\nACCEPTANCE, and it must be measured through the consumer, not at the analyzer:\nre-run measure-call-escape-cause.py on pretix and show stage 3a shrinking, AND\nreport what the sites moved TO (4a catalogue gap / 4b genuine propagating\nescape), AND report the finding-level delta in both directions. An emission-only\nor key-only win measured at the edge is exactly the capability-is-not-recall\nfailure this class was filed to prevent."  # 1937
    fields: {}  # 1937
