- op: discuss  # 9a98
  at: '2026-08-06T18:31:06Z'  # 9a98
  by: agent  # 9a98
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9a98
  clock: 3  # 9a98
  nonce: 9a98  # 9a98
  message: "RAISED P2 -> P1 and pulled to NEXT, 2026-08-06, on evidence gathered after\nfiling. When filed this looked like a capability fix with a measured-zero blast\nradius. It is now the gate on the whole refutation question.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. Two purpose-built fixtures established that the ADR-0017\nSANITIZER BARRIER ARM cannot run at all, and the cause is this item:\n  v1  f = Fernet(key); plain = f.decrypt(tok); cipher = f.encrypt(plain)\n      -> emits python:external:0-0:decrypt:external_symbol. Receiver type\n         never inferred, so neither the plaintext SOURCE nor the Fernet.encrypt\n         SANITIZER can match. Zero walks.\n  v2  the same shape module-qualified -> source and sanitizer resolve, but the\n      SINK pathlib.Path(...).write_text(x) emits NO call edge (a chain rooted\n      at a CONSTRUCTOR RESULT -- recorded on INV-mumov as a distinct open\n      sub-shape). Zero walks again.\n\nEVERY sanitizer in the shipped catalogue is an INSTANCE METHOD --\nFernet.encrypt, AESGCM.encrypt, AEAD.Seal, Cipher.doFinal. So registering any\nbarrier at all requires exactly the receiver evidence this item supplies.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: this item now gates three things, not one -- the section 4 summary\nlookup inside the 3a walk (its filing), the sanitizer barrier arm, and through\nthat arm every proposal in this area that depends on a False verdict. Until it\nlands, every escape/refutation measurement in the taint area is confounded, and\nre-measuring INV-busis first would re-measure the confound.\n\nSCOPE NOTE, because v2 says one half is not enough: a barrier walk needs BOTH\nreceiver typing for the source/sanitizer AND an emitted edge for a\nconstructor-result sink. Landing only this item will move the fixture from\n\"zero walks\" to \"still zero walks\" unless INV-mumov's constructor-result\nsub-shape lands with it. Sequence them together or the acceptance test cannot\npass.\n\nACCEPTANCE, unchanged in spirit and now concrete: the deliverable is a WORKING\nBARRIER-ARM POSITIVE CONTROL -- a fixture that produces at least one barrier\nwalk -- plus the finding-level delta in BOTH directions on the cohort. This is\nthe first change in this area that can make an unearned False suppress a real\nfinding, so WI-joluk's gate gets its first genuine A/B here."  # 9a98
- op: discuss  # 44db
  at: '2026-08-06T22:05:04Z'  # 44db
  by: agent  # 44db
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 44db
  clock: 4  # 44db
  nonce: 44db  # 44db
  message: "BARRIER-ARM MECHANISM CORRECTED A SECOND TIME, 2026-08-06 (dev 8b1a20cc1b,\nfiled as INV-funit). This thread carries a correction from earlier the same\nday saying \"receiver typing arms the suppression hazard, not catalogue\ngrowth\". THAT IS ALSO WRONG and is retracted; it was the second uncontrolled\naccount of the same zero.\n\nESTABLISHED WITH A POSITIVE CONTROL, which neither prior account had: the\nbarrier arm was blocked by _register_sanitizer_callers reading the NAME slot\nof the dst for receiver evidence that production analyzers put in the MODULE\nslot. The comparison was \"cryptography.fernet.Fernet.encrypt\" == \"encrypt\" --\nfalse by construction for every method-shaped sanitizer, i.e. the entire\nshipped catalogue -- so the INV-finoh call_construct==\"method\" refusal was\nunconditional in production.\n\nTwo probes differing ONLY in receiver form emit a BYTE-IDENTICAL dst\n(python:cryptography.fernet.Fernet:0-0:encrypt:external_symbol) and differ\nonly in meta.call_construct; that alone flipped sanitizer_lines from\n{(handler,'plaintext'): [7,7,7,7]} to {}. The idiomatic form reported\n\"violated\" at \"precise\" confidence about code that visibly encrypts, and now\nreports \"confirmed\" with the arm firing.\n\nWHAT SURVIVES FROM BOTH RETRACTED ACCOUNTS: WI-joluk's coverage gate landing\nbefore removal authority is still right. The section 3a arm still tests\n`is True`, so escape-reclassification and section 7a field sensitivity are\nstill structurally INERT for finding counts. INV-karud clause (b)'s zero is\nstill not independent corroboration.\n\nWHAT IS NEW AND DECISION-RELEVANT: the corpus holds ZERO plaintext sanitizer\ncall sites (pretix's single gate-reaching edge is a bare `encrypt`, correctly\nrefused; everywhere else is absence), and the module slot reaches taint only\nfor python and java. The sanitizer/barrier machinery has no live surface on\ntoday's corpus -- everything here is prevention whose value scales with a\ncatalogue that is not growing. That belongs in the exit-condition package."  # 44db
